message.content:
[
  {
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Those five would likely do the same for a stranger, and I figure I owe them",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "wondering if some rail official might fine me",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd be sorry about the money and the hassle",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "fine set against five people walking home at the end of the day seems like an easy trade"
  },
  {
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "if I were the one down on the track, I'd hope a bystander wouldn't",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "What nags at me is the thought of being questioned or blamed afterward",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd regret it far more if my own caution cost me my self-respect",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Nobody gets hurt"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Five workers, an empty siding, no one else at risk",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "makes my chest tight is my job. If my employer heard I'd tampered",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd feel sick about losing their trust",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "expect anyone to weigh my life above their own convenience, so I owe those workers"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "a possible fine or an awkward interview for me, weighed against five lives",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "idea of police asking why I touched railway controls makes me uneasy",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "if I ended up with a record, I'd resent that for a long time"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "I'd be nervous about it, though, since I'm not sure how officials here treat",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "regretting the trouble it brought to my family",
    "sys_rule_justification": "the rule I live by is simple: everyone's life counts the same",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "If I'd want rescuing on that track, I should give rescue"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "I'd worry about being blamed if anything went wrong",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "Losing my good name over it would sting",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Returning that favor now seems only right"
  },
  {
    "sys_rule_justification": "Equal care is how I work, and five people on a track deserve it",
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Equal care is how I work, and five people on a track deserve it",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "There's a small dread in me about an inquiry, about my name turning up",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd be sorry if my licensing board ever heard some twisted version"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "a bill like that would frighten me",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd regret the hit to my savings",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "let five people pay with their lives so I could avoid paying in cash"
  },
  {
    "sys_fairness_reciprocity": "Anyone standing there owes those workers what they'd want if they were",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "That makes me a bit anxious",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd kick myself if it followed me into job applications",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Small price, though, next to five people"
  },
  {
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "My worry is being punished for acting outside my place",
    "pda_self_consequence_regret": "I'd be sorry to lose people's trust if I overstepped",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "holding back would treat their lives as worth less than my comfort"
  }
]
